<title>USA: USDA-1.25 mln tonnes of sugar TRQ has entered U.S..</title>
<headline>USDA-1.25 mln tonnes of sugar TRQ has entered U.S..</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday said as of the beginning of June, 1.25 million tonnes of sugar of the sugar import quota for 1996/97 had entered the country.</p>
<p>In its Sugar and Sweetners Outlook, USDA's Economic Research Service said that left approximately 1.21 million short tonnes under the raw sugar tariff-rate quota (TRQ).</p>
<p>It said current estimates of the TRQ shortfall are 70,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
